      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T22:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, so during sink removal any new calls to re-allocate ports would exit early if another port\u0027s sink removal is currently executing.  This seemed like a reasonable approach to me since we\u0027d need to get up to something on the order of 4 ports total with 2 max ports before it could start causing us to not allocate another 3 A port, and we re-evaluate the sink current after things like hard or soft resets at which point a port could see that 3 A is free now.  \n\nIf we\u0027re overly concerned, we can try to synchronize things more (ex. locking when any changes are in progress).  But I hesitate to add slow-down or deadlock risk into the PD tasks.",
      "parentUuid": "be00e8d5_f784da90",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "39d087d2410bd8f3b49e06c5656b02d3e370b7a7",
