      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T21:25:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Policy outlined in your doc is to allocate 3A to the oldest port.  Need a todo here since this allocates to the lowest port number.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 426,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "39d087d2410bd8f3b49e06c5656b02d3e370b7a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "823ba578_58d2e821",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 426,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T22:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure whether giving it to the oldest port is a complication that\u0027s worth the effort anymore.  We\u0027d need to maintain 64-bit timestamps for every port\u0027s initial connection time to avoid issues with timestamp rollover, and I\u0027m not sure that either method is really going to be intuitive to a customer.  Really, the most intuitive thing for them would be if/when we can provide APIs so they can select the maximum current partner from the UI.  Thoughts? \n\nI\u0027m updating the doc for FRS soon, and could change it from \"oldest\" pretty easily.",
      "parentUuid": "a921af71_5b3bf69a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 426,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "39d087d2410bd8f3b49e06c5656b02d3e370b7a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cd09abb_9b6ee2ac",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 428,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T21:25:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is a race condition possible here? Say PD port 0 executes line 427, but then gets preempted by PD port 1.  When control comes back to PD port 0, ports_waiting will be stale.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 427,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 428,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "39d087d2410bd8f3b49e06c5656b02d3e370b7a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c0ad200_0deeaf24",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 428,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T22:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we could end up trying to re-allocate 3A to port 1 when it already snagged it itself (ex. if we were one short of the max number of ports), which should be okay.  We could also allocate to port 1 after its task had exited without allocating if we were at the max, which should also be okay.  We could also try to allocate to port 1 after it had detached, which would be okay in terms of external behavior but could leave us with a stale claimed port.  \n\nWhat are you thinking for solutions?",
      "parentUuid": "3cd09abb_9b6ee2ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 427,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 428,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "39d087d2410bd8f3b49e06c5656b02d3e370b7a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
